WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.050
Let’s learn about the main groups of PsA medicines.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:07.830
Medicines have different jobs.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:15.140
Some, like over-the-counter anti-inflammatory and pain medicines, help ease pain and swelling.

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:20.910
For milder disease, a steroid shot may be given into a sore joint.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:23.950
Doctors use the lowest dose that helps.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.920
Other medicines aim to control the disease process. These are called DMARDs.

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:36.410
That means they work to slow or stop damage, not just to ease pain.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.500
Conventional DMARDs are pills that calm the immune system in a broad way.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:49.140
Biologics target specific immune messages, and interrupt the signal.

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.870
They are usually given as a shot, or through a vein.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.570
Targeted synthetic drugs act on pathways inside cells.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.790
These are taken by mouth.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:06.730
These are names for groups. They do not rank drugs from good to bad.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.140
And how a drug enters the body does not tell you how well it will work for you.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:17.790
A drug is not right for every person or every domain.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:24.210
Some plans also include skin care, physical therapy, or help with daily tasks.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.800
Some of these medicines need infection checks before and during treatment.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.590
Ask about blood tests, infection checks, and vaccines that go with your plan.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:41.650
This lesson does not tell you to start, stop, or change a medicine.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.140
Stopping treatment because you feel well could lead to a flare, so always ask your provider first.

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:51.750
Keep your follow-up visits, even when you feel better.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:58.560
Make a list of all your medicines and supplements, and ask what each one is for.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:02.630
Great job! Let’s review.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:05.210
Medicines have different jobs.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.130
They do not rank drugs from good to bad.
